# Anthriq EXG sample recordings

Two short EEG recordings, published so that the analysis scripts in
Anthriq-algorithms can be run against real data rather than only against
synthetic signals.

## What is here

| Task | Date | Channels | Rate | Epochs |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| alpha | 2026-01-07 | O1, O2 | 1000 Hz | 6 |
| ssvep | 2026-04-14 | O1, O2, Fpz, StimTrig | 3125 Hz | 6 |

**alpha** — eyes closed against eyes open, three times. The occipital alpha
rhythm appears when the eyes close and largely disappears when they open.

**ssvep** — a square flickering at 17 Hz, fifteen seconds at a time with rest
between. The occipital response follows the stimulus frequency. The `StimTrig`
channel carries the flicker itself, one pulse per cycle, so the stimulus rate
can be confirmed independently of the EEG.

## Recording

Dry electrodes at the 10-20 positions listed above, referenced to Cz with the
ground at T7. Signals were amplified before digitisation; the values here are
referred back to the electrode, in volts as BIDS requires. Mains is 50 Hz.

Epoch onsets were recovered from a digital line that pulses at the start of
every epoch, so the times in `events.tsv` are measured rather than assumed
from the intended schedule.

## Subject

One adult subject, who recorded the sessions and consented to their public
release. No demographic information is included.

